# `STObject` Binary Wire Specification & Canonical Logic

An `STObject` represents a serialized collection of typed fields. A top-level object ends when its input is exhausted and does not append its own terminator. An object carried as a field inside another object or array is framed by the field header and the object end marker `0xE1`.

## 0. JSON Schema & Wire Mapping Table

| JSON Property | C++ Symbol / Source | Wire Framing / Bytes | Direction & Trap / Invariant Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `name` | `field->getFName().fieldName` | N/A (metadata) | Resolved via `SField::getField(type, field)` on decode, `getFName()` on encode. |
| `header` | `field->addFieldID(s)` | 1 to 3 bytes | Field ID header: `(type << 4) \| field` for common types. |
| `vl` | `Serializer::addVL` | 1 to 3 bytes | **Length Prefix**: Length prefix for VL fields (`Blob`, `AccountID`, etc.) using thresholds 192 / 12480 / 918744. Distinct from header and value. |
| `value` | `field->add(s)` | $N$ payload bytes | Raw value payload in hexadecimal. |
| `fields` | `STObject::getSortedFields(obj)` | Ordered fields list | **Encode**: Sorted ascending by `fieldCode` ($(\text{type} \ll 16) \mid \text{field}$).<br>**Decode**: Read sequentially, checks for duplicate fields via `std::adjacent_find` in `STObject::set`. |
| `elements` | `STArray::v_` | Ordered elements list | Array members (ordered list of `STObject` items, distinct from `fields` for objects). |
| `end_marker` | `s.addFieldID(sType, 1)` | `0xE1` (Object) / `0xF1` (Array) | Real nested-scope terminator represented in protocol definitions as `ObjectEndMarker` / `ArrayEndMarker`. The serializer assembles the byte from type 14 or 15 and field number 1. |
| `parts` | `STAmount::getJsonDebug` | N/A (decomposed) | Semantic discriminated union breakdown of compound types (`xahau-codec` debug extension). |

