## 1. Deserialization (`STObject::set`)

When deserializing from a `SerialIter`:
- Field IDs (`(type, field)`) are read sequentially.
- `NOP` padding markers (`type == 9 && field == 9`) are skipped. The counter
  throws when incremented to 64, so at most 63 are accepted.
- A nested object terminates when the object end marker (`type == STI_OBJECT && field == 1` $\to$ `0xE1`) is encountered; a top-level object terminates when the iterator is exhausted.
- Enforces strict canonical invariants: duplicate field detection via adjacent find on sorted fields.

