## 2. Serialization & Field Sorting (`STObject::add`)

When serializing to binary:
1. **Canonical Field Ordering**: All fields present in the object are sorted strictly ascending by `fieldCode`:
   $$\text{fieldCode} = (\text{fieldType} \ll 16) \mid \text{fieldValue}$$
2. Each field writes its `FieldID` header, followed by its payload serialization (`field->add(s)`).
3. After a nested `STObject` or `STArray` field payload, the containing object appends its real termination marker (`0xE1` for Object, `0xF1` for Array). A top-level `STObject::add` call has no surrounding field and therefore adds no final marker for itself.

